hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16061","Isam ibn Khalid narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq al-Hamdani narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Dhu al-Jawshan, he said, I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after he finished with the people of Badr, with the son of a mare of mine, and I said, O Muhammad, I have brought you the son of al-Arja to take it. He said: I have no need of it, but if you wish, I compensate you for it with the choicest of the coats of mail of Badr. So I said, I would not compensate you today with a lame one. He said: So I have no need of it. Then he said: O Dhu al-Jawshan, will you not accept Islam, so you are of the first of this affair. I said: No. He said: Why. I said: I saw your people infatuated with you. He said: So how did the news of their deaths at Badr reach you. He said, I said, it reached me. He said, I said, if you overcome Makkah and settle it. He said: Perhaps, if you live, you will see that. He said, then he said: O Bilal, take the man's bag and provision him of ajwah dates. And when I turned away, he said: He is of the best of Banu Amir. He said, so by Allah, I was with my family at al-Ghawr when a rider came, and I said, from where, he said, from Makkah. So I said, what did the people do, he said, Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has overcome it. He said, I said, may my mother be bereaved of me, so by Allah, had I accepted Islam that day, then asked him for al-Hirah, he would have granted it to me."
"16062","Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, they said, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Dhu al-Jawshan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it. He said, Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, he said, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Dhu al-Jawshan Abu Shimmar al-Dibabi, the like of this hadith. Sufyan said, and the son of Dhu al-Jawshan was a neighbor of Abu Ishaq, I do not see but he heard it from him."
